    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By definition, the functor corresponding to an edge $f: \Delta ^1 \rightarrow S$ has a left adjoint if and only if the pullback $X \times _{S} \Delta ^1 \rightarrow \Delta ^1$ is a coCartesian fibration. In other words, condition $(2)$ is equivalent to the assertion that for every edge $f: s \rightarrow s'$ and every vertex $\widetilde{s}$ of $X$ lifting $s$, there exists a <em>locally</em> $p$-coCartesian edge $\widetilde{f}: \widetilde{s} \rightarrow \widetilde{s}'$ lifting $f$. Using Corollary <a href="/tag/D4A82A" data-tag="D4A82A">5.2.2.4</a>, we conclude that $\widetilde{f}$ is automatically $p$-coCartesian, so that $(2)$ is equivalent to $(1)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
